789005368530,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"The DB has 23 enterprises total, but the park overview API says 16. The API's getEntList returns total 16. So the API filters somehow. Let me figure out the filter. Perhaps it filters by park_base_info_id = '1907044704644624386'? Let's count:\n\nEnterprises with park_base_info_id = '1907044704644624386':\n1. 兴阳化工科技有限公司 - 1907044704644624386\n2. 塞上阳光测试公司 - 1907044704644624386\n3. 天津弘羊生物工程技术有限公司 - 1907044704644624386\n4. 天源迪科遮天有限公司 - 1907044704644624386\n5. 汉威智慧安全演示企业 - 1907044704644624386\n6. 河南聚合农业科技股份有限公司 - 1907044704644624386\n7. 测试天津石化公司... - 1907044704644624386\n8. 测试数据同步功能 - 1907044704644624386\n9. 璞烯晶新材料（舟山）有限公司 - 1907044704644624386\n10. 自动化测试专用企业 - 1907044704644624386\n11. 自动化测试专用企业2 - 1907044704644624386\n\nThat's 11. Hmm, not 16.\n\nMaybe the 16 comes from a different source. Note the API list included: 汉威智慧安全演示企业, 自动化测试专用企业, 河南粮油置业, 兴阳化工科技, 测试数据同步功能, 润广石化测试公司, 璞烯晶新材料, 测试天津石化公司, 塞上阳光测试公司, 天津弘羊生物工程技术有限公司 — that's 10 shown. Total 16.\n\nHmm, the API records include 河南粮油置业 (park_base_info_id=null in DB), 润广石化测试公司 (null). So the API filter isn't park_base_info_id.\n\nMaybe the tenant is different. Let me check: the API is /park/overopen/getEntList for park overview. It might filter by tenants belonging to the park. Actually, maybe it filters by `in_park` or by a tenant list.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. Maybe there's a different table. Let me check what table the getEntList uses — perhaps `park_base_info_ent` or there's a mapping table. Let me search for tables that could hold \"入驻企业\". \n\nActually let me think differently: rather than reverse-engineering, the DB query of ent_businessinfo_info gives 23 rows, but the API says 16. There might be a `register_status` filter (审核状态0未审核1审核通过)? Let's check register_status values.\n\nActually, let me look at this more carefully. Let me check tenant_id — maybe only enterprises with certain tenant_ids count.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Looking at the API response more carefully: the ent list API returned records that seem to be from a different set. Let me check whether there's a \"park_base_info\" table with ent relationship.\n\nLet me be pragmatic: query with more fields including register_status, tenant_id, create_time to see the 23 and figure out the 16.\n\nActually — maybe the discrepancy: the API counts enterprises where in_park='1'? Let's count in_park='1':\n1. 中原汇通科技 - 1\n2. 中圣石油科技 - 1\n3. 汉威智慧安全演示企业 - 1\n4. 河南汉威智慧安全科技 - 1\n5. 河南粮油置业 - 1\n6. 河南聚合农业科技 - 1\n7. 自动化测试专用企业 - 1\n8. 英吉森科技 - 1\n\nThat's 8. Not 16.\n\nHmm. Let's count tenants. Maybe \"16\" is the count of企业 in a specific park, but the DB has multiple parks? park_base_info_id is 1907044704644624386 for 11 of them.\n\nHmm, 16 ≠ 11, 23, 8.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the API uses a different table entirely, e.g., `park_base_info_ent` join. Let me look for a table linking park and ent. Let me grep the spilled table list for \"park_base\".\n\nActually, the spilled mysql_tables output was truncated but included a full list of tables matching '%ent%'/'%company%'. There's no park_base_ent table in that list.\n\nLet me query the actual API's data source differently — maybe check `ent_businessinfo_info` where tenant_id is in the set of tenants bound to the park.\n\nAlternative approach: get the distinct tenant_ids and compare with the 10 known enterprises from the API to figure out the filter.\n\nLet me query: SELECT id, ent_name, tenant_id, register_status, business_status, create_time, park_base_info_id, in_park FROM ent_businessinfo_info ORDER BY create_time.\n\nLet me do that.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the situation. The user asked \"园区有多少家企业\" and I answered 16 based on the API. The user said \"需要\" (yes, needed) to my offer of: full 16-name list + chart by risk/industry.\n\nThe cleanest path: figure out which 16 the API counts. Let me get tenant_ids of the 10 known ones and see.\n\nKnown 10 tenant_ids:\n- 汉威智慧安全演示企业: 1907019009553985537\n- 自动化测试专用企业: 1926910356154769409\n- 河南粮油置业: 2069619899275173890\n- 兴阳化工科技: 1909566100666908673\n- 测试数据同步功能: 1913101817301004290\n- 润广石化测试公司: 1914572060422664193\n- 璞烯晶新材料: 1914639861715922946\n- 测试天津石化: 1914649251068080129\n- 塞上阳光测试公司: 1914863140464586754\n- 天津弘羊生物: 2018200158782648321\n\nLet me query ent_businessinfo_info for all with tenant_id and see which 16 match a pattern. Let me look at whether these tenant_ids are a contiguous/special set.\n\nLet me just query all 23 with tenant_id, register_status, create_time.\n\nI'll also query the count of ent_businessinfo_info grouped by something.\n\nLet's run a broad query.\n\nActually — a thought: maybe the park overview list uses table `ent_businessinfo_info` but with a tenant filter from the park's tenants. And the \"16\" total might include the 10 + 6 more that are in a second \"page\" that the API can't return.\n\nLet me just enumerate: which 16? Let's see if there's a table `sys_tenant` and the park binds certain tenants.\n\nLet me run a query joining to find the answer. First let's see the raw data with tenant info.\n\nLet me do multiple queries in parallel:\n1. SELECT id, ent_name, tenant_id, register_status, create_time, park_base_info_id, in_park, business_status FROM ent_businessinfo_info ORDER BY create_time\n2. Check if there's a table with 'base_info' in name (park_base_info).\n\nLet me run query 1."}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1789005368530,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"数据库里企业表有 23 条，而园区总览 API 统计口径是 16 条。让我核对一下口径。"}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1789005368531,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_bnras6RuAxDmz34HuzAC7091","name":"mysql_query","arguments":"{\"sql\": \"SELECT id, ent_name, tenant_id, register_status, company_status, business_status, in_park, park_base_info_id, industrial_park_name, create_time FROM ent_businessinfo_info ORDER BY create_time, ent_name\"}"}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1789005368531,"chunk":{"