call_01_WtjK1gxxR0DRwuAAZnGP5357","name":"mysql_query","args":["","{","\"","sql","\"",": ","\"","SELECT"," *"," FROM"," park","_base","_info","\"","}"]},{"type":"chunk","time":1789005378851,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now, the API getEntList returned 16. Let me figure out the filter. Look at the 10 returned in API page1:\n汉威智慧安全演示企业 (create 2025-03-31)\n自动化测试专用企业 (2025-05-25)\n河南粮油置业 (2026-06-23)\n兴阳化工科技有限公司 (2025-04-07)\n测试数据同步功能 (2025-04-17)\n润广石化测试公司 (2025-04-21)\n璞烯晶新材料（舟山）有限公司 (2025-04-21)\n测试天津石化公司... (2025-04-21)\n塞上阳光测试公司 (2025-04-22)\n天津弘羊生物工程技术有限公司 (2026-02-01)\n\nNot returned: 河南汉威智慧安全科技, 测试化工园区企业, 园区四五八预发布测试, 企业测试测试企业, 天源迪科遮天有限公司, 汉威福特然软件公司, 自动化测试专用企业2, 新疆天山畜牧..., 河南聚合农业科技, 中原汇通科技, 中圣石油科技, 中化二建集团, 英吉森科技 = 13.\n\n10 + 13 = 23. ✓\n\nHmm so 16 total from API but only 10 shown. So 6 more that are neither in the 10 shown nor... wait, 23 - 10 = 13 others, of which 6 are counted by the API. So the API's filter selects 16 out of 23.\n\nWhat distinguishes them? Let's look at returned ones: all have `park_base_info_id` OR ... hmm 河南粮油置业 has park_base_info_id=null, 润广石化测试公司 null too. But all returned ones have industrial_park_name? No: 河南粮油置业 has \"化工园区\", 润广 has null.\n\nHmm. Let's look at tenant_id magnitude/prefix. Returned tenant_ids:\n1907019009553985537\n1926910356154769409\n2069619899275173890\n1909566100666908673\n1913101817301004290\n1914572060422664193\n1914639861715922946\n1914649251068080129\n1914863140464586754\n2018200158782648321\n\nNot returned:\n2018553969703415809 (河南汉威智慧安全科技)\n1907038941108891649 (测试化工园区企业)\n1930070221438119937\n1930581220431818753\n1930580493697347586 (天源迪科)\n1932270409401573378\n1937751898444599298 (自动化测试专用企业2)\n1947891828449685506\n2018925107285618690 (河南聚合农业)\n2069606084873576450 (中原汇通)\n2069592940604317697 (中圣石油)\n2089638858607079426 (中化二建)\n2089559419483357185 (英吉森)\n\nHmm. This is getting complicated. Maybe the park overview uses a different source: maybe `park_base_info` has tenant list, or the API filters by `park_base_info_id IS NOT NULL OR industrial_park_name IS NOT NULL`? Let's test: those with park_base_info_id not null = 11 (listed earlier). Plus industrial_park_name not null: 汉威智慧安全演示企业(already), 中原汇通科技, 中圣石油科技, 河南粮油置业 (already). So 11 + 3 = 14. Not 16.\n\nHmm, close but not 16.\n\nWait, let me recount park_base_info_id = '1907044704644624386':\n1. 汉威智慧安全演示企业\n2. 兴阳化工科技有限公司\n3. 测试数据同步功能\n4. 测试天津石化公司...\n5. 璞烯晶新材料（舟山）有限公司\n6. 塞上阳光测试公司\n7. 自动化测试专用企业\n8. 天源迪科遮天有限公司\n9. 自动化测试专用企业2\n10. 天津弘羊生物工程技术有限公司\n11. 河南聚合农业科技股份有限公司\n\n= 11. Plus industrial_park_name='化工园区': 中原汇通科技, 中圣石油科技, 河南粮油置业 (汉威智慧安全演示企业 already counted). = 3 more → 14.\n\nStill 14, not 16. And note 自动化测试专用企业2 and 天源迪科 and 河南聚合农业 are in the 14 but NOT in the API's returned page-1 list. So the filter is not that.\n\nHmm, so maybe the API's 16 is based on tenant-level data joined with something else.\n\nOK. Let me step back and think about what's practical.\n\nRather than fully reverse-engineering, I could look at what makes the 16. Since the API can't page, maybe I can request with a filter parameter. query_module supports `filter`. The API getEntList likely accepts entName filter. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively — maybe I'm overcomplicating. Perhaps the discrepancy is because the park overview \"allCount\" counts something else (e.g., includes non-enterprise tenants). \n\nLet me look at this from a different angle: check `sys_tenant` for tenants that are enterprises of the park. Or check `park_base_info` table.\n\nActually, maybe the \"16\" comes from a tenant list where tenant has `del_flag=0` and `company_type` etc.\n\nHmm, let me try a completely different approach: use query_module with a filter to see if I can get more info, OR check if the getEntList API accepts pageSize larger than 10 — the api_count is 16 APIs; pageSize 50 didn't work for search_enterprises either (it returned 10, total 16, pageSize 50 echoed). That suggests the backend caps at 10... Actually search_enterprises echoed pageSize:50 but returned 10 records — server-side max limit.\n\nHmm wait, actually the response said `\"total\":16,\"pageNo\":1,\"pageSize\":50` but records has 10. That's odd — it echoed my params. So the backend ignores them and returns a fixed 10.\n\nLet me try mysql: maybe there IS a query the API uses. Let me look at park_base_info table content.\n\nLet me query park_base_info.\n\nAlso, maybe the answer: the API counts tenants in `sys_tenant` linked to park. Let me check sys_tenant.\n\nLet me look at park_base_info first.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider — maybe the enterprise table used by getEntList isn't ent_businessinfo_info but a tenant-based query on sys_tenant where the user list... \n\nLet me check sys_tenant.\n\nLet me run a few queries.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the numbers: 23 total enterprises in ent_businessinfo_info. API says 16. Difference 7.\n\nHmm, what if the API counts enterprises whose tenant_id corresponds to a \"企业\" tenant type? \n\nLet me just query sys_tenant.\n\nLet me also consider: maybe getEntList is filtered by park's tenant scope where `park_base_info_id` matches OR the tenant is in the park's enterprise tenant list stored elsewhere.\n\nLet's get park_base_info row and sys_tenant rows.\n\nI'll run these.\n\nActually — maybe simpler and more valuable: I should just report the discrepancy honestly and give the full list from the DB (23) with a note, plus the API's 16. But the user wants the 16 complete list. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — perhaps I should look at the dict/tables. Let me check if there's a table specifically listing park enterprises: search for tables like '%park_ent%'.\n\nFrom the list: park_run_ent (企业分类分级监管配置表), park_report_entdata, park_property_management, park_base_info. \n\n`park_run_ent` — 企业分类分级监管配置表! That might be the list of enterprises under the park's supervision. Let me check its content.\n\nLet me query park_run_ent and park_base_info."}}},{"type":"chunk","time":178900537885